/**
 * @mainpage dmosal
 *
 * A small, portable embedded C abstraction layer providing deterministic/bounded
 * resource management and consistent concurrency, timing, and communication
 * semantics across POSIX and RTOS platforms.
 *
 * This page indexes the API reference below. For narrative documentation, see
 * the Markdown docs in `docs/` (also linked from the project README):
 *
 * - architecture.md &mdash; layered design, subsystem overview, resource-manager
 *   pattern, callback threading model, backend model.
 * - thread-safety.md &mdash; per-API table classifying every public call as
 *   thread-safe, single-owner, or init-thread-only.
 * - lifetime.md &mdash; init/deinit ordering, resource ownership, when it is
 *   safe to use/release a resource.
 * - api-spec.md &mdash; behavioral specification per subsystem: functions,
 *   states, error codes, invariants.
 * - porting.md &mdash; how to add a new backend (e.g. an RTOS or bare-metal
 *   target).
 */
